Tester 49441, pair 182205 (conv 48589): „სანტექნიკოსი … ჰკითხე ილია
ტესტაძეს და ნოდარ ტესტაძეს." typed in a new conversation was bound to the
open goal of the first conversation (the same need). Asks under a goal that
lives in another conversation are refused (askedFromAnotherGoalsThread),
so ask_contact was refused three times, „call create_task first", and only
one of the two was asked.

An order to ask named people is the request of the conversation it is
typed in. The repeat check is skipped for such a line, and it opens its
own goal here. The server's own send (instructedAsk.goalFor) no longer
files it under another conversation's goal either.

DONE WHEN: 3928 run 2 on 2 fresh pairs, the first goal working or waiting
— both named people asked, and the owner told who it went to.

